+---
+id: PLAN-012-sessions-search-box
+status: draft
+date: 2026-11-05
+review_count: 0
+patch: n/a
+---
+
+# PLAN-012: Search box on the Sessions page
+
+## Status
+
+draft
+
+## Context
+
+The user asked: "the sessions page needs a search box".
+
+`web/src/pages/Sessions.tsx` renders every `SessionSummary` returned by
+`GET /api/sessions` in a single table. There is no way to narrow the list;
+once the session count grows, finding a past recording means scanning rows
+by eye. The list endpoint returns the full set with no query parameters,
+and each summary already carries the fields a user would plausibly search
+by: id/slug, date, languages, STT provider, model, and speaker names.
+
+No clarifications were requested per the task instruction; assumptions are
+recorded under Risks and notes.
+
+## Governing records
+
+- BDR-001: personal single-user tool; session volume is personal scale
+  (hundreds of files at most), so client-side filtering over the
+  already-fetched list is sufficient. No pagination or server-side query
+  is needed.
+- BDR-002: zero new dependencies and zero runtime cost - the filter runs
+  in the browser over data the page already loads.
+- ADR-001: this is a frontend-internal concern; the REST and WebSocket
+  surfaces are unchanged.
+- ADR-007 (supersedes ADR-004): session discovery is a filesystem
+  listing, O(file count), already paid by `listSessions`. ADR-004's
+  consequences name a SQLite index as the designated next step *if
+  cross-session (full-content) search is ever needed*. This plan is
+  metadata-only filtering; full transcript content search stays out of
+  scope and would require its own record.
+- ADR-006: TypeScript strict; shadcn policy for UI primitives (the
+  existing `web/src/components/ui/input.tsx` is reused - no `shadcn add`
+  needed); vitest for unit tests; `oxlint` for the web lint gate.
+
+## Scope
+
+In scope:
+
+1. A search input on the Sessions page that filters the rendered table
+   rows as the user types.
+2. A small pure helper module (`web/src/lib/session-search.ts`) holding
+   the matching logic so it is unit-testable.
+3. Unit tests for the helper; existing suites untouched.
+
+Out of scope: backend/API changes (no query params, no new endpoints),
+searching transcript `.srt`/`.md` body content (full-text search),
+searching assist notes, debouncing or indexing (unnecessary at this
+volume), persisting the query across navigation, and changing any column
+or row behavior.
+
+## Design decisions (pinned)
+
+**Matching semantics**: case-insensitive substring match on a single
+trimmed query. One query string, no tokenization, no operators. Empty or
+whitespace-only query matches everything. A session matches when the
+lowercased query appears anywhere in a haystack built from:
+
+- `s.id` (the slug shown in the Session column, e.g. `standup-1430`)
+- `s.file` (the stored relative path; catches date-folder fragments like
+  `2026-11-05`)
+- `s.started_at` (raw ISO string; date fragments like `11-05` match)
+- `s.source_lang` and `s.target_lang`
+- `s.stt_provider` and `s.model` (null-safe)
+- `Object.values(s.speakers)` (renamed speaker display names are
+  searchable)
+
+The localized date string rendered in the Started column is deliberately
+NOT in the haystack: `toLocaleString()` output is environment-dependent
+and would make the helper non-deterministic in tests.
+
+**Helper contract** (`web/src/lib/session-search.ts`, new file):
+
+```ts
+import type { SessionSummary } from './types';
+
+export function sessionMatches(s: SessionSummary, query: string): boolean;
+export function filterSessions(
+  sessions: SessionSummary[],
+  query: string,
+): SessionSummary[];
+```
+
+- `sessionMatches` builds the lowercased haystack once per call and
+  returns `haystack.includes(q)` where `q = query.trim().toLowerCase()`;
+  `q === ''` returns `true` early.
+- `filterSessions` is `sessions.filter((s) => sessionMatches(s, query))`
+  and preserves input order (the server already returns newest first).
+
+**Page changes** (`web/src/pages/Sessions.tsx`):
+
+- New state: `const [query, setQuery] = useState('')`.
+- Derived rows:
+  `const filtered = useMemo(() => filterSessions(sessions, query), [sessions, query])`.
+  No debounce: the array is small and the filter is a few string scans.
+- Placement: `CardHeader` becomes a flex row
+  (`flex items-center justify-between gap-3`); `CardTitle` unchanged on
+  the left; the search control on the right. The control is a
+  `relative` wrapper (`w-56 sm:w-64`) containing:
+  - a `Search` lucide icon (`size-4`, `text-muted-foreground`,
+    absolutely positioned at the left edge, `pointer-events-none`),
+  - the existing shadcn `Input` with `pl-8` (room for the icon),
+    `placeholder="Search sessions"`, `aria-label="Search sessions"`,
+    `value={query}`, `onChange={(e) => setQuery(e.target.value)}`,
+  - when `query !== ''`, a clear button: `Button` `variant="ghost"`
+    `size="icon"` absolutely positioned at the right edge holding an `X`
+    lucide icon, `aria-label="Clear search"`, `onClick={() => setQuery('')}`.
+- The table body maps `filtered` instead of `sessions`. Row content is
+  unchanged (Live badge, Review and Live buttons).
+- No-match state: when `filtered.length === 0`, the body renders one
+  `TableRow` whose `TableCell` has `colSpan={7}` and
+  `className="py-8 text-center text-muted-foreground"` containing
+  `No sessions match "{query}"`. The header row stays visible so the
+  column context is not lost.
+- The early `sessions.length === 0` `Empty` return stays as-is: with no
+  sessions at all there is nothing to search, so the card (and the input)
+  is not rendered.
+
+**Icons**: `Search` and `X` added to the existing `lucide-react` import.
+
+## Steps
+
+### Step 1 - `web/src/lib/session-search.ts` (new)
+
+Implement `sessionMatches` and `filterSessions` per the pinned contract.
+Keep the haystack construction in a private function so the field list
+lives in exactly one place.
+
+### Step 2 - `web/src/pages/Sessions.tsx`
+
+- Import `useMemo`, `Search`/`X` icons, the `Input` component, and
+  `filterSessions`.
+- Add `query` state and the `filtered` memo.
+- Restructure `CardHeader` per the pinned layout and render the table
+  over `filtered` with the no-match row.
+
+### Step 3 - `web/src/lib/session-search.test.ts` (new)
+
+Vitest suite covering the cases in the test plan below. Build
+`SessionSummary` fixtures literally in the test file (the type is a flat
+record; no factory exists to reuse).
+
+## Test plan
+
+Automated (`web/src/lib/session-search.test.ts`, vitest):
+
+- empty string and whitespace-only query return the input list unchanged.
+- match is case-insensitive (`STANDUP` matches id `standup-1430`).
+- matches on: id substring, `file` path fragment (`2026-11`),
+  `started_at` ISO fragment, `target_lang`, `stt_provider`, `model`, and
+  a speaker display name from `speakers`.
+- non-matching query returns an empty array.
+- `filterSessions` preserves the input order of matches.
+- `model: null` and `speakers: {}` do not throw and simply do not match.
+
+Gates: `npm run typecheck`, `npm test`, `npm --prefix web run build`,
+`npm --prefix web run lint`.
+
+Manual acceptance:
+
+- On `/sessions`, typing a slug fragment narrows the table; clearing via
+  the X button restores all rows.
+- A query with no matches shows the "No sessions match" row with all 7
+  column headers still visible.
+- With zero sessions the page still shows the "No sessions yet" empty
+  state and no search box.
+- Filtering does not hide or break the Live badge or the Review/Live
+  buttons on matching rows.
+
+## Risks and notes
+
+- Assumption: "search box" means filtering the session list by its
+  visible metadata, not full-text search over transcript bodies. If the
+  user meant the latter, that is a different feature (per ADR-004's
+  designated SQLite-index path) and needs its own ADR/plan - flagged
+  here so the gap is explicit.
+- The localized Started column text (e.g. `11/5/2026, 2:30 PM`) is not
+  searchable; ISO fragments (`2026-11-05`, `11-05`) are. If users search
+  by spoken-month dates ("Nov 5"), extending the haystack with a
+  deterministic formatted date is a small follow-up.
+- The query is page-local state: navigating to a session and back resets
+  it. Acceptable for this iteration; `sessionStorage` persistence would
+  be a trivial follow-up if requested.
+- Speaker names are only searchable after they exist in frontmatter;
+  unlabeled sessions still match on `Speaker 1`-style keys only via
+  `Object.values`, which hold display names - original labels
+  (`Speaker 1`) are keys, not values, so a search for `speaker 1` will
+  not match. Considered acceptable; matching on keys too would produce
+  surprising hits across every diarized session.
+- No performance concern: O(sessions x haystack length) per keystroke at
+  personal volume. If the list ever grows large, a 150 ms debounce is
+  the obvious escalation, not an index.
+
+## Definition of Done
+
+- [ ] `web/src/lib/session-search.ts` exports `sessionMatches` and
+  `filterSessions` with the pinned semantics.
+- [ ] Sessions page shows a search input in the card header that filters
+  rows live, with a clear button when the query is non-empty.
+- [ ] No-match queries render the single `colSpan=7` "No sessions match"
+  row; zero-session state unchanged.
+- [ ] `web/src/lib/session-search.test.ts` covers the cases above and
+  passes.
+- [ ] Gates clean: `npm run typecheck`, `npm test`,
+  `npm --prefix web run build`, `npm --prefix web run lint`.
+- [ ] Manual acceptance list verified in the browser.
-- 
2.50.0


